I checked the project memory: queues are separated by channel (one queue for email, one for SMS, one for push) — decision recorded here: viking://user/default/memories/events/2026/08/11/Separate queues per channel.md.

Main reason: isolate channels so that a traffic spike or an issue on one channel does not slow down or block the others. Practical benefits:
- independent scalability for each channel;
- channel-specific retry/backoff policies and SLAs;
- simpler monitoring and capacity planning;
- isolation of failures/outages of external providers.
